{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310723,"nonce":"WDm1rANwNKh2mGp+1DBW2U0DEfo=","title":"FIXED — switch-as-expression with multi-statement let-bound case body now extracts trailing expression as the case's value (was silently ...","message":"**Status: FIXED in tast_to_hir.rs's case-body lowering.**\n\n**Original symptom**: switch-as-expression with a multi-statement\ncase body silently exited (no SIGSEGV stack, just disappeared)\nwhen the case body had `var \u003cname\u003e = …; \u003ctrailing-expr\u003e;` shape:\n\n```haxe\nvar size:Int = switch (dtype) {\n    case 14:\n        var nBlocks = Std.int(nElem / 256);   // ← Let stmt\n        nBlocks * 144;                         // ← trailing expr (case's value)\n    case _: -1;\n};\ntrace(\"after\");      // never printed\n```\n\n**Root cause**: The TAST→HIR lowering at `tast_to_hir.rs:2519+`\n(constructor-pattern path) and `tast_to_hir.rs:2580+`\n(literal-pattern → if-chain path) only handled\n`TypedStatement::Expression` as the case body's value source. A\nmulti-statement case body is parsed as `TypedStatement::Expression\n{ expression: TypedExpressionKind::Block { statements } }` — the\nBlock wraps the multi-stmt sequence and its trailing expression IS\nthe case's value. The original code just lowered the Block as a\nside-effecting expression statement, so the trailing expression\nnever bound back to the switch's result temp (or never became the\nif-chain's branch value). The result temp kept its\ntype-appropriate default (0 / 0.0 / false / null), and downstream\nreads got garbage that often manifested as a silent exit when\nused in further arithmetic / control flow.\n\n**Fix**: two new helpers in `tast_to_hir.rs` —\n`lower_case_body_to_assign(body, result_symbol)` and\n`lower_case_body_to_expr(body, result_ty)` — each unwrap the\n`Expression { Block { … } }` shape, split off the trailing\n`Expression` statement, lower the leading statements in order,\nand emit an assignment (or set the block's trailing `expr`)\nusing the lowered trailing expression. Falls back to the old\nsingle-statement path for non-block bodies.\n\n**Verified**:\n- Standalone repro (`/tmp/test_switch_let/Main.hx`) now prints\n  correct values (e.g. `nBlocks * 144 = 147750912`).\n- Haxe regression: 127/128 (same documented `test_exception`\n  SIGTRAP flake; no new regressions).\n- nue/examples/tiny-transformer still passes.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_switch_expr_null_init]] (prior fix: temp init\nvalue type-correct, which addressed constructor patterns with\nprimitive result types). This fix completes the picture for the\n*value-source* side: a multi-stmt block now produces the right\nvalue, not just the right initial default.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_switch_with_let_field_scrutinee` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}